riousness-category collection in one study scenario.","candidate_statement_id":"proposal-sdtmig34-gold-ae-example1-v1","expected_statement":"The example demonstrates free-text AE collection, MedDRA coding, optional term modification, and seriousness-category collection in one study scenario.","expected_statement_id":"stmt-sdtmig34-ae-example1","review_required":true},{"candidate_statement":"For RELTYPE=MANY, apply the published erratum that uses --LNKGRP rather than --LNKID for IDVAR.","candidate_statement_id":"proposal-sdtmig34-gold-erratum-lnkgrp-v1","expected_statement":"Apply the published erratum: a RELTYPE=MANY row uses --LNKGRP rather than --LNKID for IDVAR.","expected_statement_id":"stmt-sdtmig34-erratum-lnkgrp","review_required":true},{"candidate_statement":"Read AE.AEENRF values together with the general relative-timing guidance in Section 4.4.7.","candidate_statement_id":"proposal-sdtmig34-gold-aeenrf-crossref-v1","expected_statement":"Interpret allowable AEENRF codelist values together with the general relative-timing guidance in Section 4.4.7.","expected_statement_id":"stmt-sdtmig34-aeenrf-crossref","review_required":true}]}
